{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016qzauEaE7drh4Y2jjwTGGH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Spec: issue 1, the README has no \"run it\" section\n2\t\n3\t## Outcome\n4\t\n5\tA volunteer who opens `README.md` can start the web page, run the desk CLI and run the tests by\n6\tcopying commands from one short section.\n7\t\n8\t## Requirements\n9\t\n10\t- The system shall have a section in `README.md` whose heading is \"Run it\".\n11\t- When a reader looks in the \"Run it\" section for the web page, the system shall show the command `bun src/server.ts`.\n12\t- When a reader looks in the \"Run it\" section for the desk CLI, the system shall show a command that starts with `bun src/desk.ts` and name the `overdue` command.\n13\t- When a reader looks in the \"Run it\" section for the tests, the system shall show the command `bun test`.\n14\t- Where the section names a script file, the system shall name a file that exists in the app.\n15\t\n16\t## Must not change\n17\t\n18\t- Nothing under `src/` changes.\n19\t- Nothing under `tests/` that exists today changes.\n20\t- The \"Folders\" table in `README.md` stays as it is.\n21\t- `package.json` stays as it is.\n22\t\n23\t## Out of scope\n24\t\n25\t- Adding a `desk` or `start` script to `package.json`.\n26\t- Installing Bun or the dependencies.\n27\t- Describing the seed data or the web page's API.\n28\t\n29\t## Done when\n30\t\n31\t- `bun run gate` exits 0 with the new tests passing.\n32\t- The new tests in `tests/docs/readme.test.ts` pass.\n33\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69731084-f4db-49de-ac0b-b241bf229bd6","uuid":"bc77fd7e-cebb-4300-8804-d6e227195110","timestamp":"2026-11-13T05:05:59.758Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/user/software-factory-claude-code/parts/06-price-and-ship/03-ship-the-factory/solution/runs/1/repo/specs/1/SPEC.md","content":"# Spec: issue 1, the README has no \"run it\" section\n\n## Outcome\n\nA volunteer who opens `README.md` can start the web page, run the desk CLI and run the tests by\ncopying commands from one short section.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- The system shall have a section in `README.md` whose heading is \"Run it\".\n- When a reader looks in the \"Run it\" section for the web page, the system shall show the command `bun src/server.ts`.\n- When a reader looks in the \"Run it\" section for the desk CLI, the system shall show a command that starts with `bun src/desk.ts` and name the `overdue` command.\n- When a reader looks in the \"Run it\" section for the tests, the system shall show the command `bun test`.\n- Where the section names a script file, the system shall name a file that exists in the app.\n\n## Must not change\n\n- Nothing under `src/` changes.\n- Nothing under `tests/` that exists today changes.\n- The \"Folders\" table in `README.md` stays as it is.\n- `package.json` stays as it is.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Adding a `desk` or `start` script to `package.json`.\n- Installing Bun or the dependencies.\n- Describing the seed data or the web page's API.\n\n## Done when\n\n- `bun run gate` exits 0 with the new tests passing.\n- The new tests in `tests/docs/readme.test.ts` pass.\n","numLines":33,"startLine":1,"totalLines":33}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016qzauEaE7drh4Y2jjwTGGH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
